k7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"gVGOy2ACwZMMKyMZFxVAPQ","review_id":"A-kvQ1elSN1j9nusRrAtUw","date":"2016-04-20T18:17:46","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9310303330421448,"text_excerpt":"I actually really like the pita pit. It's exactly what it sounds like - pitas and some other things on the menu. I have never dined in, just ordered take out three or four times. Every time the food is consistently good, and matches the online menu (at least what I've ordered). The service is always fast and the people working in there are nice. I'll definitely be back."},{"business_id":"gVGOy2ACwZMMKyMZFxVAPQ","review_id":"FBwKME8NHA2O7fmxZFfsyw","date":"2009-02-26T15:50:50","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9299522042274475,"text_excerpt":"I love me some Pita Pit. It beats Subway, for sure. Lots of different meat and veggie options, including hummus and falafal for veg*ns. The only issue with this place is the parking, but it's on Magazine Street, so I wouldn't expect a huge parking lot anyway. Bonus points for being near Whole Foods, so I can grab a pita either before or after doing my grocery shopping for the week."},{"business_id":"gVGOy2ACwZMMKyMZFxVAPQ","review_id":"gK0IamnB6fvx6HdL_lB40w","date":"2011-07-25T19:59:17","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9242943525314331,"text_excerpt":"This is my late-night go to food option. Out of the whole area, this place delivers the latest. I love that they use fresh ingredients and cook your food when you order. You can expect to spend about $10 for your pita and soda. But even on my hungriest of days, I always walk away happy and full."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"gVGOy2ACwZMMKyMZFxVAPQ","photo_id":"pJIsQmSVZGkJw4ge2RVWKQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/pJIsQmSVZGkJw4ge2RVWKQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0}]},"notebook_case":null}
